  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1133 PM CDT Fri Jul 10 2026\n\nForecast models continue to depict high pressure shifting to the\nnorth over the next few days. We will end up on the southern end\nof this high pressure ridge by the later part of the weekend and\nearly next week. Embedded disturbances are expected to circulate\nacross the southern end of the ridge. This will provide enough\nsupport for thunderstorm development. In fact, rain chances are \nhigh (around 70%) in the Monday and Tuesday timeframe in \nparticular. Given ample moisture remaining in place, there remains\na Marginal Risk (5 to 15% chance) of excessive rainfall leading to\nflash flooding both days. By the middle of next week, the high\npressure center appears to drift back to the south and southwest\nresulting in lower rain chances and hotter temperatures for the \nlater part of the week.",
